  m_Name: 1930s kaya
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Kaya Toast and Kopi 1930s
  info: "Introduced by Hainanese immigrants working as cooks in British households,
    kaya toast became a popular breakfast staple. It consists of bread slathered
    with kaya (coconut jam) and butter, accompanied by soft-boiled eggs and a strong
    cup of kopi (local coffee). This simple yet iconic meal is a nostalgic reminder
    of Singapore\u2019s colonial past and cultural ingenuity.  "
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1c6bae48f1a1947199cc01971b7bbcc3, type: 3}
